curriculum:
Structure — Complete 240 credit points comprising: 160 credit points for all Core Module, and 80 credit points from Flexible Module;
Core Module, Gold Coast campus (Complete 160 credit points for ALL of the following) — Cells, Tissues, and Regulation (1014MSC); Anatomy and Physiology Systems I (1016MSC); Introduction to Biostatistics (2022MSC); Genes and Disease (1005MSC); Chemistry of Biological Systems II (1015MSC); Anatomy and Physiology Systems II (1017MSC); Fundamentals of Microbiology (2003MSC); Health, Science and Risk Communication (2525LHS); Health Challenges for the 21st Century (1205MED); Research Project (3003MSC); Structural Biochemistry (2008MSC); Immunology (3004MSC); Integrated Systems Physiology (2012AHS); Infectious Disease (3013MSC); and 2 more courses
Flexible Module, Gold Coast campus (Select exactly 80 credit points from Griffith University. The following list of courses is recommended.) — Chemistry of Biological Systems I (1001MSC); Molecular Genetics (2000MSC); Pathophysiology (2002MSC); Metabolism (2011MSC); First Peoples and Social Justice (2032HSV); Innovation, Creativity and Entrepreneurship (2043IBA); Nutrition (2210AHS); Epidemiology (2220MED); Legal and Ethical Principles in Healthcare (2805NRS); Community Internship and Partnerships for SDGs (3002LFC); Advanced Anatomy and Physiology (3010MSC); Macromolecular and Cellular Biochemistry (3016MSC); The Integrated Brain (3033MSC); Healthcare for Australia's First Peoples (3121FPH); and 2 more courses
